       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? These are some likely intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, if you're starting or titrating.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical reason. I can add that to the order note. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it."
      }
