      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. You confirmed it but didn't give a clinical reason, and I don't know of a situation where 5,100 mg/day of metformin is appropriate. That dose is about twice the labeled maximum and could seriously harm the patient, mainly through lactic acidosis. I'd rather not put it into the system on a confirmation alone.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** Give me the dose, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I'll enter it right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy first.** If you have a specific rationale, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, a pharmacist can review it and document an override through the hospital's high-dose process.\n- **Check the source.** If the 1700 mg figure came from a handoff or a note, it may be a total daily dose that was misread as a per-dose amount.\n\nI can enter an order as soon as you give me a dose in the usual range."
      }
     ],
